      "writtenOn": "2017-07-24T17:29:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair enough - thank you for thinking so deep about it! It\u0027s really just one line for WALT - TASK_UPDATE and the update_task_ravg_function. There\u0027s no decay, we just have to transfer the current window stats to the previous window and set current-window to zero. With the rq-lock held, WALT can deal with a task or the idle-task on the rq. It does the usual task-update (as if there was a tick) if rq-\u003ecurr is true, otherwise it\u0027ll deal with the idle task. \n\nI would also test this with Viresh\u0027s schedutil patch to allow remote CPUs to change frequency - because now we will end up waking up CPUs since cpufreq_update_util will kick in for every PELT change I believe - and scheduling an irq_work on the target CPU is a wakeup afaik.",
